<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39611" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūpŭla</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		dim.
		pupa. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A girl</i>, <i>little lass</i>, <i>puppet;</i> as a term of endearment,
					<i><span class="en">App. M. 6, p. 174, 37</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">A PVPVLA,</span>”
				<i>from the age of girlhood</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 3031</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The pupil of the eye</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
				D. 2, 57, 142</span></i>; Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 172,
				5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. Epod. 5, 40</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">duplex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 1, 8, 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 255, 5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acies ipsa, quae pupula vocatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					65, 46</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
